'''National Securities Depository Limited (NSDL)'''  is an Indian [[central securities depository]], based in [[Mumbai]]. It was established in August 1996 as the first electronic securities depository in India with national coverage.<ref>{{Cite web |title=About Us - NSDL |url=https://nsdl.co.in/about/index.php |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20060213221806/http://www.nsdl.co.in/about/index.php |archive-date=2006-02-13 |access-date=2024-01-18 |website=NSDL}}</ref> As of 2025, its [[demat account]]s held assets worth ₹464 lakh crore ($4.64 trillion).<ref>{{Cite web |date=2023-12-31 |title=Statistics - NSDL |url=https://nsdl.co.in/about/statistics.php |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240118182648/https://nsdl.co.in/about/statistics.php |archive-date=2024-01-18 |access-date=2024-01-18 |website=NSDL}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Desk|first=B. Q.|title=Assets In NSDL Demat Accounts Now Worth $4 Trillion|url=https://www.bloombergquint.com/business/assets-in-nsdl-demat-accounts-now-worth-4-trillion|access-date=2022-01-17|website=BloombergQuint|date=23 October 2021 |language=en}}</ref><ref name=":0" /><ref name=":1">{{Cite web|title=What is NSDL service?|url=https://www.businessinsider.in/what-is-nsdl-service/articleshow/70669034.cms|access-date=2022-01-17|website=Business Insider|archive-date=17 January 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220117155509/https://www.businessinsider.in/what-is-nsdl-service/articleshow/70669034.cms|url-status=dead}}</ref>

NSDL provides services to investors, stock brokers, custodians and issuer companies through a network of [[Depository participant|Depository Participants]] and digital platforms. Its services are related to [[Dematerialization (securities)|dematerialization]], [[Stock transfer agent|transfer]] and [[Settlement (finance)|settlement]] of securities in the Indian securities market.

==History==
National Securities Depository Limited (NSDL) is an Indian central securities depository under the jurisdiction of Ministry of Finance, Government of India based in Mumbai. The enactment of [[Depositories Act|Depositories Act, December 1995]] paved the way for establishment of NSDL as Joint-Venture of PSUs and PSBs. It was established in 1996 as the first electronic securities depository in India with national coverage.

NSDL has more than 2.80 crore demat accounts as of 30 June 2022. It contributes to majority of the settlement in the Indian securities markets and has more than 89% share in the total value of assets held in demat form in India.{{citation needed|date=October 2022}}

The [[initial public offering]] (IPO) of NSDL was launched in July 2025 as an offer for sale (OFS) of shares worth ₹4,012 crore (US$458 million) by its existing shareholders, including [[National Stock Exchange of India|NSE]], [[IDBI Bank]], [[State Bank of India]], [[HDFC Bank]], and SUUTI. The shares listed on [[Bombay Stock Exchange|BSE]] on 6 August 2025.<ref>{{cite web | last1=M | first1=Vivek Kumar | last2=Monnappa | first2=Chandini | last3=Mukherjee | first3=Hritam | last4=Monnappa | first4=Chandini | last5=Mukherjee | first5=Hritam | title=NSDL's $458 million India IPO fully sold within hours of launch | work=Reuters | date=30 July 2025 | url=https://www.reuters.com/world/india/nsdls-458-million-india-ipo-fully-sold-within-hours-of-launch-2025-07-30/ }}</ref><ref>{{cite web | title=NSE, banks to offload 5 cr NSDL shares in IPO | work=The Times of India | date=24 July 2025 | url=https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/business/india-business/nse-banks-to-offload-5-cr-nsdl-shares-in-ipo/articleshow/122878661.cms }}</ref><ref>{{cite web | title=NSDL IPO: Issue opens on July 30, here's what you need to know about GMP, issue details - NSDL's Upcoming IPO | url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/nsdl-ipo-issue-opens-july-30-heres-what-you-need-to-know-about-gmp-issue-details/nsdls-upcoming-ipo/slideshow/122931933.cms }}</ref>

==Company structure==
NSDL Group comprises National Securities Depository Limited (abbreviated as NSDL), NSDL Database Management Limited (NDML) and NSDL Payments Bank Limited. NDML and NSDL Payments Bank are two subsidiary companies of NSDL.

